1
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:08,850
Are you sure about this?

2
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,550
No.

3
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:13,620
It's dangerous.

4
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:18,220
If we take Tywin's castle from him,

5
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:21,530
the lords of Westeros will realize he's not invincible.

6
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,030
Take his home,

7
00:02:23,130 --> 00:02:25,160
take his gold, take his power.

8
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,300
Why are you telling me?

9
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,340
You begged me not to send Theon to negotiate with his father

10
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:36,780
and I ignored your advice.

11
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:41,110
Now Winterfell is burnt to the ground,

12
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:43,320
the North is overrun with ironborn,

13
00:02:43,350 --> 00:02:45,420
and Bran and Rickon are gone.

14
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,820
So Casterly Rock...

15
00:02:54,290 --> 00:02:56,130
I'm asking your advice.

16
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:04,400
We have enough men?

17
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:10,240
If Walder Frey cooperates.

18
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:13,250
If Walder Frey cooperates.

19
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:21,450
If reinforcements arrive from King's Landing

20
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:23,860
before we take the castle...

21
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:29,060
we'll be caught between Tywin's army and the sea.

22
00:03:33,330 --> 00:03:36,830
We'll lose the war and die the way Father died.

23
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:38,870
Or worse.

24
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:47,710
Show them how it feels to lose what they love.

25
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:20,510
My honored guests...

26
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:24,580
be welcome within my walls

27
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,420
and at my table.

28
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:31,120
I extend to you my hospitality

29
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:34,990
and protection in the light of the Seven.

30
00:04:35,030 --> 00:04:37,660
We thank you for your hospitality, my lord.

31
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:44,500
I have come to make my apologies, my lord,

32
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:46,400
and to beg your forgiveness.

33
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:49,810
Don't beg my forgiveness, Your Grace.

34
00:04:51,210 --> 00:04:54,350
It wasn't me you spurned. It was my girls.

35
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:09,530
One of them was supposed to be queen.

36
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,230
Now none of them are.

37
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:15,800
This is Arwyen my daughter.

38
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:20,440
My daughter Walda, my daughter Derwa,

39
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:23,040
my daughter Waldra.

40
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,780
My eldest granddaughters

41
00:05:29,810 --> 00:05:33,120
Ginia and Neila.

42
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:39,190
Serra and Sarra, granddaughters, twins.

43
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,790
You could have had either.

44
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:44,090
Could have had both for all I care.

45
00:05:44,130 --> 00:05:46,560
My granddaughter Marianne.

46
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,470
My granddaughter Freya.

47
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,300
My granddaughter...

48
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,940
Wertha.

49
00:05:57,170 --> 00:06:00,240
Waldra.

50
00:06:00,310 --> 00:06:02,280
Waldina.

51
00:06:02,350 --> 00:06:05,110
- I'm Merry. - Fine.

52
00:06:05,150 --> 00:06:08,920
And here's my youngest daughter Shirei,

53
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:11,890
though she hasn't bled yet.

54
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,790
Clearly you don't have the patience for all that.

55
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,790
My ladies.

56
00:06:17,830 --> 00:06:21,330
All men should keep their word, kings most of all.

57
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:25,900
I was pledged to marry one of you and I broke that vow.

58
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:28,100
The fault is not with you.

59
00:06:28,170 --> 00:06:31,540
Any man would be lucky to have any one of you.

60
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:34,480
I did what I did not to slight you,

61
00:06:34,510 --> 00:06:36,350
but because I loved another.

62
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,280
I know these words cannot set right

63
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,350
the wrong I have done to you and your house.

64
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:43,690
I beg your forgiveness

65
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:46,820
and pledge to do all I can to make amends

66
00:06:46,890 --> 00:06:49,690
so the Freys of the Crossing and the Starks of Winterfell

67
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,660
may once again be friends.

68
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,870
Very good.

69
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:05,010
There she is.

70
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,180
Come closer.

71
00:07:07,210 --> 00:07:09,180
Let me have a look at you.

72
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,320
Still can't see you.

73
00:07:18,350 --> 00:07:20,490
Old eyes.

74
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:37,370
Love.

75
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:41,280
That's what the Starks of Winterfell call it, eh?

76
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,420
Very honorable.

77
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:47,720
I call it a pretty face.

78
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:50,820
Mmm, very pretty.

79
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,030
Prettier than this lot, that's for sure.

80
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,630
Very shapely as well.

81
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:03,330
Oh, you try to hide her under that dress.

82
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:05,340
If you wanted to hide her,

83
00:08:05,370 --> 00:08:07,740
you shouldn't have brought her here in the first place.

84
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:15,410
I can always see

85
00:08:15,450 --> 00:08:18,280
what's going on beneath a dress.

86
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:21,220
Been at this a long time.

87
00:08:22,490 --> 00:08:25,120
I bet when you take that dress off,

88
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:27,860
everything stays right where it is.

89
00:08:27,890 --> 00:08:29,690
Doesn't drop an inch.

90
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:35,230
Your king says he betrayed me for love.

91
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:38,000
I say he betrayed me for firm tits

92
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:40,640
and a tight fit.

93
00:08:40,670 --> 00:08:43,340
And I can respect that.

94
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:48,380
When I was your age, I'd have broken 50 oaths

95
00:08:48,410 --> 00:08:51,850
to get into that without a second thought.

96
00:08:55,250 --> 00:08:58,650
Well, I've enough room in the hall for you lot.

97
00:08:58,690 --> 00:09:00,760
We'll set up tents outside

98
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:03,160
with food and ale for the rest of your men.

99
00:09:03,190 --> 00:09:05,360
Thank you, my lord.

100
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,200
Well, let's get ready.

101
00:09:10,230 --> 00:09:12,270
The wine will flow red

102
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:15,770
and the music will play loud

103
00:09:15,810 --> 00:09:20,010
and we'll put this mess behind us.

104
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:30,720
Where?

105
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,360
There.

106
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:42,330
There. It's a back gate.

107
00:09:42,370 --> 00:09:45,270
My men use it when they visit Yunkai's bed slaves.

108
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:47,000
Your men, but not you?

109
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,670
I have no interest in slaves.

110
00:09:48,710 --> 00:09:50,980
A man cannot make love to property.

111
00:09:54,210 --> 00:09:55,880
This is where we enter the city.

112
00:09:55,950 --> 00:09:57,380
Very few guards. They know me.

113
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:58,920
They let me inside--

114
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:01,190
We're not gonna sneak an army through a back gate.

115
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:04,190
I kill the guards. I take your two best men

116
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:07,590
and lead them through the back streets, which I know well,

117
00:10:07,630 --> 00:10:09,730
and open the front gates.

118
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:11,360
Then comes the army.

119
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:14,030
Once the walls are breached, the city will fall in hours.

120
00:10:14,070 --> 00:10:16,970
Or perhaps you'll lead Grey Worm and me to the slaughter,

121
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,470
cutting the head off our army.

122
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:22,240
The masters of Yunkai will pay you your fee

123
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,640
and you won't have to split it three ways

124
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,680
'cause you've already slaughtered your partners.

125
00:10:25,710 --> 00:10:28,180
You have a very suspicious mind.

126
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:31,290
In my experience, only dishonest people think this way.

127
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,660
You command the Unsullied.

128
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:38,140
What do you think?

129
00:10:50,870 --> 00:10:52,040
You leave tonight.

130
00:10:52,070 --> 00:10:54,170
Very good.

131
00:10:54,210 --> 00:10:56,010
We'll prepare.

132
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,720
Ser Jorah.

133
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:06,420
You can use an extra sword.

134
00:11:06,450 --> 00:11:08,960
You're the Queensguard, Ser Barristan.

135
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:11,020
Your place is by the queen.

136
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:13,490
If we are truly her loyal servants,

137
00:11:13,530 --> 00:11:15,560
we'll do whatever needs to be done

138
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:19,730
no matter the cost, no matter our pride.

139
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,310
We're west of Castle Black,

140
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:27,340
but the Nightfort's closest to us.

141
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:30,510
It was the first castle on the Wall.

142
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:33,950
The Watch abandoned it during the reign of King Jaehaerys I.

143
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:37,650
Too big. Impossible to maintain.

144
00:11:37,690 --> 00:11:40,020
Other than Castle Black itself,

145
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:42,520
the Nightfort's the perfect castle for us.

146
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:46,030
It's got a secret sally port,

147
00:11:46,090 --> 00:11:48,660
the Black Gate, as old as the Wall itself.

148
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:52,430
No one's used it in centuries most likely.

149
00:11:52,470 --> 00:11:55,130
It leads through the Wall

150
00:11:55,170 --> 00:11:57,070
right down into the Nightfort,

151
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:58,970
if one knows how to find it,

152
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:01,910
which, it just so happens, I do.

153
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:09,250
How do you know all that?

154
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:13,220
I read about it in a very old book.

155
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:23,260
You know all that from staring at marks on paper?

156
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:26,330
Yes.

157
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:29,130
You're like a wizard.

158
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:46,320
Our father used to tell us

159
00:12:46,350 --> 00:12:50,720
that no wildling ever looked upon the Wall and lived.

160
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:53,260
Here we are.

161
00:12:53,330 --> 00:12:55,630
Alive.

162
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:14,650
Remember what happens to children who run.

163
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,520
I'm your father and I'll do the talking.

164
00:13:27,430 --> 00:13:29,760
The roads have gone right to hell, haven't they?

165
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,930
Cracked three spokes this morning.

166
00:13:31,970 --> 00:13:33,970
- Need a hand? - Need about eight hands.

167
00:13:35,970 --> 00:13:38,140
Got to get this salt pork to the Twins

168
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:40,780
in time for the wedding.

169
00:13:40,810 --> 00:13:43,310
Many thanks.

170
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,050
Don't!

171
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,380
Don't kill him.

172
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:50,590
Dead rats don't squeak.

173
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:52,290
You're so dangerous, aren't you?

174
00:13:52,350 --> 00:13:54,360
Saying scary things to little girls.

175
00:13:54,390 --> 00:13:57,160
Killing little boys and old people.

176
00:13:57,230 --> 00:13:58,630
A real hard man you are.

177
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,630
More than anyone you know.

178
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:03,400
You're wrong. I know a killer.

179
00:14:03,430 --> 00:14:06,070
- A real killer. - That so?

180
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,700
You'd be like a kitten to him.

181
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:10,070
He'd kill you with his little finger.

182
00:14:10,110 --> 00:14:12,210
That him?

183
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:15,610
- No. - Good.

184
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:18,580
Don't kill him.

185
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:20,880
Please.

186
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:23,050
Please don't.

187
00:14:25,690 --> 00:14:27,750
You're very kind.

188
00:14:27,790 --> 00:14:29,760
Someday it'll get you killed.

189
00:14:47,110 --> 00:14:48,940
Where are we?

190
00:14:49,010 --> 00:14:51,180
The Gift, I think.

191
00:14:51,210 --> 00:14:52,850
Brandon the Builder gave all this land

192
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,950
south of the Wall to the Night's Watch

193
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,920
for their sustenance and support.

194
00:14:57,950 --> 00:15:00,220
Maester Luwin taught me that.

195
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:04,290
Doesn't seem to be supporting anyone at the moment.

196
00:15:04,330 --> 00:15:08,030
It's good land and there's no war up here.

197
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:09,560
Why leave?

198
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:11,300
Wildlings.

199
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:13,070
Sorry.

200
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:15,800
But they come over the Wall and raid,

201
00:15:15,870 --> 00:15:17,670
steal, carry off women.

202
00:15:17,710 --> 00:15:19,910
Old Nan said they turn your skull into a cup

203
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:22,010
and make you drink your own blood from it.

204
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:26,380
That's what Old Nan said.

205
00:15:26,410 --> 00:15:28,080
There's a storm coming.

206
00:15:29,450 --> 00:15:31,750
I don't see any.

207
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:36,960
It's as good a place to shelter as any.

208
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:42,560
We can drink some blood while we wait.

209
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:44,730
I don't need much.

210
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:58,980
Only one old man and eight good horses.

211
00:15:59,050 --> 00:16:02,120
What's one old man doing with eight horses?

212
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:04,020
He breeds them for the Watch.

213
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:06,020
How's he keep folks from stealing them?

214
00:16:06,050 --> 00:16:08,390
The Watch protects him.

215
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:10,660
Not today they don't.

216
00:16:10,690 --> 00:16:13,360
He's selling horses, he's got some gold in there.

217
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,600
- And proper steel. - Let's carve him up.

218
00:16:16,630 --> 00:16:18,000
We just take the horses and go.

219
00:16:18,030 --> 00:16:20,700
The old man's no threat.

220
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:23,170
I keep telling you.

221
00:16:23,210 --> 00:16:25,340
He's an old man.

222
00:16:25,370 --> 00:16:27,840
A spear through the heart's a better way to die

223
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:30,280
than coughing up your last with no one but your horses to hear.

224
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:35,220
The Watch might send a few men looking for a horse thief.

225
00:16:35,250 --> 00:16:38,120
They'll send a lot more to hunt down murderers.

226
00:16:38,150 --> 00:16:39,990
I hope so.

227
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:42,960
Killing crows in their castle is tough.

228
00:16:42,990 --> 00:16:44,930
Killing them out here in the open,

229
00:16:44,990 --> 00:16:46,660
that's what we do.

230
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,430
Spread out.

231
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:51,030
Surround the hut and move in.

232
00:17:33,810 --> 00:17:35,040
Ygritte!

233
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:39,610
Clear the barn!

234
00:18:16,790 --> 00:18:19,490
No one's going to believe you're a hog farmer if you eat them all.

235
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,520
Best part of the animal.

236
00:18:27,230 --> 00:18:29,430
Don't worry. They're still there.

237
00:18:30,670 --> 00:18:32,270
I know they're still there.

238
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:34,040
You check every five minutes

239
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:36,640
like you're afraid they're gonna move.

240
00:18:36,670 --> 00:18:38,440
I'm not afraid.

241
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,710
Of course you are.

242
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:43,050
You're almost there

243
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:45,680
and you're afraid you won't make it.

244
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:49,120
The closer you get, the worse the fear gets.

245
00:18:49,150 --> 00:18:52,590
No point in trying to hide behind that face.

246
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:55,530
I know fear when I see it.

247
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,430
Seen it a lot.

248
00:18:58,730 --> 00:19:01,260
I knew fear when I saw it in you.

249
00:19:02,730 --> 00:19:05,540
You're afraid of fire.

250
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:07,310
When Beric's sword went up in flames,

251
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:09,170
you looked like a scared little girl.

252
00:19:12,810 --> 00:19:15,150
And I know why, too.

253
00:19:17,020 --> 00:19:19,450
I heard what your brother did to you.

254
00:19:20,590 --> 00:19:21,890
Pressed your face to the fire

255
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:24,520
like you're a nice juicy mutton chop.

256
00:19:28,330 --> 00:19:30,500
That give you some ideas?

257
00:19:33,330 --> 00:19:36,000
Might do.

258
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:38,370
Go ahead, then.

259
00:19:38,410 --> 00:19:40,770
You might get away.

260
00:19:40,810 --> 00:19:43,340
Might even make it there on your own.

261
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:46,650
They're just over the river.

262
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,820
The closest you've been to family

263
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:51,880
since Ilyn Payne snipped your daddy's neck.

264
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:58,320
Someday I'm gonna put a sword through your eye

265
00:19:58,360 --> 00:19:59,990
and out the back of your skull.

266
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:28,150
How are we going to get past the Wall?

267
00:20:28,190 --> 00:20:30,120
My uncle said it's 700 feet high.

268
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:37,030
How did you get past it?

269
00:20:41,070 --> 00:20:43,800
Got in a boat and rowed past the Bay of Seals.

270
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:47,040
It would take us two months to get to the Bay of Seals.

271
00:20:47,070 --> 00:20:49,210
Some climb straight up the ice.

272
00:20:49,270 --> 00:20:50,380
Even Hodor's not strong

273
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:52,540
enough to climb the Wall with me on his back.

274
00:20:52,610 --> 00:20:55,780
Hodor.

275
00:20:55,810 --> 00:20:58,350
19 castles guard the Wall.

276
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:01,750
- Only three are still manned. - Hodor!

277
00:21:01,790 --> 00:21:04,020
One of those abandoned fortresses will give us a way through.

278
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:06,290
My uncle said the gates were sealed with ice and stone

279
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:07,760
when the castles were deserted.

280
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:10,190
Well, we'll have to open them up again.

281
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:15,030
There's a rider out there.

282
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:18,670
Just one?

283
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:20,470
- There's more. - Hodor!

284
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:26,110
- It's just thunder, sweet giant. - Hodor.

285
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:28,510
I yield.

286
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:30,210
- I yield. - Wildlings.

287
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:36,820
Where's Shaggydog and Summer?

288
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:38,860
Hunting.

289
00:21:38,930 --> 00:21:40,890
Hodor!

290
00:21:40,930 --> 00:21:43,230
- Quiet, Hodor. - Hodor!

291
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:45,260
Make him shut up. If they hear us...

292
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:47,470
- Hush, Hodor. No more Hodoring. - Hodor!

293
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:50,400
- Hodor! - Hodor, calm down.

294
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,770
- You need to keep quiet. - They're gonna hear us.

295
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:53,970
Hodor, be quiet.

296
00:21:55,580 --> 00:21:57,640
- Ah! Hodor! - Hodor, calm down.

297
00:21:57,710 --> 00:22:00,680
- Hodor! Hodor! - Hodor, be quiet!

298
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:24,640
What did you do?

299
00:22:24,670 --> 00:22:27,410
Nothing.

300
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:29,370
I don't know.

301
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,080
What's that?

302
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,580
That's a horse dying.

303
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:51,230
Bring them over here.

304
00:22:51,260 --> 00:22:54,430
That was the last of them. The rest are dead.

305
00:22:54,470 --> 00:22:56,700
I heard shouting up there.

306
00:22:56,740 --> 00:22:58,870
Thunder.

307
00:22:58,900 --> 00:23:01,470
I know the difference between shouting and thunder.

308
00:23:01,510 --> 00:23:04,640
Maybe it's ghosts.

309
00:23:14,550 --> 00:23:16,890
That won't help you, grandpa.

310
00:23:21,260 --> 00:23:22,930
Where you riding?

311
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,960
Doesn't matter now, does it?

312
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,730
No, it doesn't matter now.

313
00:23:29,430 --> 00:23:32,840
Cut his throat or he'll tell the crows we're here.

314
00:23:38,740 --> 00:23:40,480
You understand.

315
00:23:40,510 --> 00:23:42,480
Let me stand at least.

316
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:45,920
Let me go with a bit of dignity.

317
00:23:50,950 --> 00:23:52,660
Make the crow kill him.

318
00:23:56,190 --> 00:23:59,600
You're one of us now. Prove it.

319
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:06,400
The wolves are out there.

320
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:11,040
I can't do it by choice.

321
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:15,110
I don't know how. It happens in my dreams.

322
00:24:15,150 --> 00:24:16,860
You're a warg, Bran.

323
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:19,350
It's in your blood.

324
00:24:19,940 --> 00:24:20,980
I can't.

325
00:24:21,220 --> 00:24:22,680
You just did with him.

326
00:24:23,220 --> 00:24:24,630
A wolf is nothing compared to that.

327
00:24:33,030 --> 00:24:34,390
She looks sharp.

328
00:24:44,300 --> 00:24:45,310
Do it.

329
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:47,920
Do it.

330
00:24:48,690 --> 00:24:51,060
I told you. He's still one of them.

331
00:24:53,790 --> 00:24:55,050
Go on, boy.

332
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,370
Go on!

333
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:10,100
He's a crow.

334
00:25:10,290 --> 00:25:11,910
He'll always be a crow.

335
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:14,330
And here's his crow wife guarding him.

336
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:17,340
He'll stab us in the back first chance he gets.

337
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:21,520
Kill him.

338
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:39,740
- He's one of them. - No!

339
00:25:40,490 --> 00:25:41,470
Do you hear me?

340
00:25:48,410 --> 00:25:50,660
You're not gonna die for one of them.

341
00:25:52,870 --> 00:25:54,100
Do it.

342
00:25:55,690 --> 00:25:57,380
They'll find us if you don't.

343
00:26:27,130 --> 00:26:28,930
You were right the whole time.

344
00:27:16,290 --> 00:27:18,340
When you hear a songbird's whistle, you come.

345
00:27:18,890 --> 00:27:21,750
I'm a great whistler. The greatest in the land.

346
00:27:28,210 --> 00:27:29,840
Daario Naharis.

347
00:27:58,700 --> 00:28:00,160
That one was quick.

348
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:05,450
- There may be others. - I doubt it.

349
00:28:05,670 --> 00:28:08,250
The Yunkish prefer to let their slaves do their fighting for them.

350
00:28:53,130 --> 00:28:55,160
That's what you call a few guards?

351
00:29:20,210 --> 00:29:21,720
Come on! What do you got, huh?

352
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:37,970
Lord Edmure...

353
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:42,800
I hope I'm not a disappointment to you.

354
00:30:52,090 --> 00:30:54,030
You're a delight to me, my lady.

355
00:30:55,900 --> 00:30:57,270
You may now cloak the bride

356
00:30:57,270 --> 00:30:59,270
and bring her under your protection.

357
00:31:28,650 --> 00:31:29,870
In the sight of the Seven,

358
00:31:30,780 --> 00:31:33,380
I hereby seal these two souls,

359
00:31:34,180 --> 00:31:37,420
binding them as one for eternity.

360
00:31:37,730 --> 00:31:40,230
Look upon each other and say the words.

361
00:31:43,300 --> 00:31:47,660
Father, Smith, warrior, Mother,

362
00:31:47,660 --> 00:31:50,520
Maiden, Crone, Stranger...

363
00:31:51,570 --> 00:31:52,890
- I am hers... - I am his...

364
00:31:53,300 --> 00:31:54,760
- and she is mine... - and he is mine...

365
00:31:55,310 --> 00:31:59,010
...from this day until the end of my days.

366
00:32:03,840 --> 00:32:06,490
- Is that safe? - They're long gone.

367
00:32:12,060 --> 00:32:13,070
You were right.

368
00:32:13,290 --> 00:32:15,850
I can get inside Summer's mind whenever I want.

369
00:32:16,590 --> 00:32:17,700
Of course you can.

370
00:32:19,410 --> 00:32:21,080
North of the Wall there are wildlings

371
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,130
who can control all sorts of animals.

372
00:32:24,750 --> 00:32:26,520
But you did a lot more than that.

373
00:32:28,460 --> 00:32:30,320
You got inside Hodor's mind.

374
00:32:32,580 --> 00:32:34,380
They can't do that north of the Wall?

375
00:32:36,710 --> 00:32:39,670
No one can do that... anywhere.

376
00:32:46,700 --> 00:32:48,410
When I was looking through Summer's eyes,

377
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:50,730
- I saw Jon. - Where?

378
00:32:50,730 --> 00:32:52,420
He was with the wildlings.

379
00:32:52,580 --> 00:32:54,530
They tried to kill him, but he got away.

380
00:32:54,530 --> 00:32:56,460
He'll be heading back to Castle Black, then.

381
00:32:56,980 --> 00:32:58,280
That's where we should go.

382
00:32:58,440 --> 00:33:00,900
For all we know, Castle Black's already under attack.

383
00:33:01,140 --> 00:33:03,250
- If this many wildlings got through-- - I already told you.

384
00:33:03,850 --> 00:33:05,880
I'm not going north of the Wall.

385
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:08,680
Everything Jojen told me is true.

386
00:33:10,630 --> 00:33:12,790
You saw what I did to Hodor.

387
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,860
I have to find the three-eyed raven.

388
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:16,310
Listen to me, little lord.

389
00:33:16,310 --> 00:33:17,130
Don't worry.

390
00:33:18,470 --> 00:33:20,540
I'm not asking you to come with me.

391
00:33:22,690 --> 00:33:24,500
It won't be safe for Rickon.

392
00:33:25,130 --> 00:33:27,570
Me? I'm coming with you.

393
00:33:27,570 --> 00:33:28,260
No.

394
00:33:29,690 --> 00:33:32,590
You and Osha and Shaggydog head for the Last Hearth.

395
00:33:32,590 --> 00:33:35,490
The Umbers are our bannermen. They'll protect you.

396
00:33:35,490 --> 00:33:37,280
I'm coming with you.

397
00:33:37,970 --> 00:33:39,290
I'm your brother.

398
00:33:39,840 --> 00:33:41,470
I have to protect you.

399
00:33:44,130 --> 00:33:46,700
Right now I have to protect you.

400
00:33:47,580 --> 00:33:50,290
Robb's at war and I'm going beyond the Wall.

401
00:33:50,700 --> 00:33:52,480
If something happens to us,

402
00:33:52,480 --> 00:33:54,430
you're the heir to Winterfell.

403
00:33:57,010 --> 00:33:59,100
Would you know how to find the Last Hearth?

404
00:33:59,100 --> 00:34:02,230
You southerners build your big castles and you never move.

405
00:34:02,590 --> 00:34:04,010
You're easy to find.

406
00:34:04,540 --> 00:34:06,500
We're not southerners.

407
00:34:07,890 --> 00:34:09,990
And I don't want to leave you.

408
00:34:09,990 --> 00:34:12,510
Come here, little soldier.

409
00:34:14,140 --> 00:34:17,110
You and me, we're gonna have some adventures.

410
00:34:18,120 --> 00:34:19,960
You don't have to do any of this.

411
00:34:21,370 --> 00:34:22,950
Your family took me in

412
00:34:22,950 --> 00:34:25,310
and was good to me when they had no cause to be.

413
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:29,630
We'll be fine, you and me.

414
00:34:30,090 --> 00:34:31,860
The Umbers are great warriors.

415
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:34,300
Even I heard about them growing up.

416
00:34:35,140 --> 00:34:37,390
They'll teach you how to swing a sword.

417
00:34:38,370 --> 00:34:40,450
I know how to swing a sword.

418
00:34:47,990 --> 00:34:50,560
You're leaving now? It's the middle of the night.

419
00:34:50,560 --> 00:34:52,630
I learned to walk in darkness.

420
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:56,850
Say your good-byes, little man.

421
00:35:04,860 --> 00:35:06,500
Keep this one safe.

422
00:35:09,090 --> 00:35:10,820
He means the world to me.

423
00:35:32,030 --> 00:35:33,870
We've been waiting a long time.

424
00:35:36,470 --> 00:35:37,550
Haven't we?

425
00:35:39,570 --> 00:35:41,000
I don't know, you tell me.

426
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:43,190
How long does it take to sack a city?

427
00:35:52,040 --> 00:35:53,760
It was just as you said.

428
00:35:54,330 --> 00:35:56,560
They did not believe until it was too late.

429
00:35:57,270 --> 00:35:59,000
Their slave soldiers

430
00:35:59,260 --> 00:36:01,940
threw down their spears and surrendered.

431
00:36:06,990 --> 00:36:09,290
And Daario Naharis?

432
00:36:30,090 --> 00:36:31,760
The city is yours, my queen.

433
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:57,030
They're good, aren't they?

434
00:36:57,160 --> 00:36:59,050
They ought to be because they cost enough.

435
00:37:06,590 --> 00:37:08,010
Look at the crowd there.

436
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:14,950
He complained about this marriage

437
00:37:14,950 --> 00:37:17,220
the entire ride from Riverrun,

438
00:37:17,380 --> 00:37:18,680
and now look at him.

439
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,110
The gods love to reward a fool.

440
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:22,930
- Uncle. - What?

441
00:37:23,430 --> 00:37:25,980
He's my nephew. I love him.

442
00:37:26,650 --> 00:37:28,610
And he's a damned fool.

443
00:37:33,790 --> 00:37:35,560
Don't you drink, Lord Bolton?

444
00:37:35,950 --> 00:37:38,410
Never do, my lady. Dulls the senses.

445
00:37:38,410 --> 00:37:39,880
That's the point.

446
00:37:40,510 --> 00:37:42,690
Didn't you marry one of these Frey girls?

447
00:37:42,690 --> 00:37:43,610
Aye.

448
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:46,460
Lord Walder let me choose any of his granddaughters

449
00:37:46,870 --> 00:37:49,850
and promised me the girl's weight in silver as a dowry.

450
00:37:50,460 --> 00:37:52,150
So I have a fat young bride.

451
00:37:54,190 --> 00:37:56,000
I hope she makes you very happy.

452
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:57,950
Well, she's made me very rich.

453
00:37:58,300 --> 00:38:00,610
Pardon, my lord, my lady.

454
00:38:00,610 --> 00:38:03,130
I need to find a tree to piss on.

455
00:38:05,500 --> 00:38:07,350
My mother's alone with Roose Bolton.

456
00:38:07,990 --> 00:38:09,080
I should rescue her.

457
00:38:09,250 --> 00:38:10,980
Your mother is less in need of rescue

458
00:38:10,980 --> 00:38:12,480
than any woman I've ever met.

459
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:13,970
Be kind.

460
00:38:14,140 --> 00:38:15,960
She's finally starting to like you.

461
00:38:17,900 --> 00:38:19,060
And I like her.

462
00:38:19,600 --> 00:38:21,350
But if she had her way,

463
00:38:21,350 --> 00:38:24,010
I would be back in Volantis playing my harp

464
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:25,760
and you would be sitting over there

465
00:38:26,380 --> 00:38:28,990
eating blackberries out of Roslin Frey's hand.

466
00:38:29,560 --> 00:38:31,670
Perhaps I've made a terrible mistake.

467
00:38:34,230 --> 00:38:37,110
Striking your king is an act of treason.

468
00:38:40,550 --> 00:38:41,920
No, don't.

469
00:38:43,780 --> 00:38:45,340
Don't insult them.

470
00:38:47,620 --> 00:38:49,160
Your Grace.

471
00:38:56,470 --> 00:38:59,700
The septon has prayed his prayers,

472
00:39:00,520 --> 00:39:02,220
some words were said,

473
00:39:02,620 --> 00:39:04,080
and Lord Edmure

474
00:39:04,450 --> 00:39:07,370
has wrapped my daughter in a cloak.

475
00:39:07,550 --> 00:39:11,370
But they are not yet man and wife.

476
00:39:11,900 --> 00:39:14,480
A sword needs a sheath.

477
00:39:20,690 --> 00:39:23,140
And a wedding needs a bedding.

478
00:39:24,390 --> 00:39:25,930
What does my sire say?

479
00:39:26,180 --> 00:39:33,460
To bed! To bed! To bed!

480
00:39:34,690 --> 00:39:36,770
If you think the time is right, Lord Walder,

481
00:39:36,770 --> 00:39:41,170
by all means, let us bed them.

482
00:39:47,740 --> 00:39:55,000
To bed! To bed! To bed!

483
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:57,680
Go on!

484
00:40:17,060 --> 00:40:19,620
Oh! Careful now, ladies.

485
00:40:19,830 --> 00:40:21,590
Once you set that monster free,

486
00:40:21,590 --> 00:40:23,350
there's no caging him again.

487
00:40:24,610 --> 00:40:29,520
To bed! To bed! To bed!

488
00:40:31,520 --> 00:40:32,680
Poor girl.

489
00:40:33,380 --> 00:40:35,220
Every bride suffers the same.

490
00:40:36,250 --> 00:40:38,670
I'm sure you endured yours with grace.

491
00:40:38,670 --> 00:40:40,120
Oh, Ned forbade it.

492
00:40:41,390 --> 00:40:42,430
He said it wouldn't be right

493
00:40:42,430 --> 00:40:44,650
if he broke a man's jaw on our wedding night.

494
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:55,540
That is a very strange custom.

495
00:40:56,530 --> 00:40:57,970
I suppose it does seem strange

496
00:40:57,970 --> 00:40:59,630
from a foreigner's perspective.

497
00:41:00,020 --> 00:41:01,390
It seems normal to you?

498
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:03,670
It's a tradition.

499
00:41:06,140 --> 00:41:08,490
Without the bedding ceremony, there's no real proof

500
00:41:08,490 --> 00:41:10,600
the lord and lady consummated their marriage.

501
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:14,470
But there are other ways of providing proof.

502
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:18,190
Boy or girl?

503
00:41:21,470 --> 00:41:22,440
I don't know.

504
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:25,920
But if it's a boy, I know what we should name him.

505
00:41:25,920 --> 00:41:27,160
Oh, do you?

506
00:41:28,470 --> 00:41:29,610
It seems to me the father

507
00:41:29,610 --> 00:41:31,680
should have some say in his son's naming.

508
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:32,820
Eddard.

509
00:41:37,040 --> 00:41:38,890
Don't you want to teach little Ned Stark

510
00:41:38,890 --> 00:41:40,370
how to ride horses?

511
00:41:41,560 --> 00:41:42,740
I do.

512
00:42:39,830 --> 00:42:41,090
Go on, line 'em up!

513
00:43:03,910 --> 00:43:05,010
Where are you going?

514
00:43:05,450 --> 00:43:07,240
Got salt pork for the feast.

515
00:43:07,240 --> 00:43:08,620
The feast is over.

516
00:43:09,970 --> 00:43:11,860
Doesn't sound like it's over.

517
00:43:11,860 --> 00:43:14,740
If I tell you it's over, it's over.

518
00:43:15,690 --> 00:43:18,070
Turn this cart around and get the hell out of here.

519
00:43:19,320 --> 00:43:20,870
Got pig's feet, too.

520
00:43:22,610 --> 00:43:24,150
Are you soft in the head?

521
00:43:24,330 --> 00:43:25,970
Turn this cart around.

522
00:43:38,810 --> 00:43:40,110
Your Grace.

523
00:43:46,420 --> 00:43:50,040
I feel I've been remiss

524
00:43:50,650 --> 00:43:52,010
in my duties.

525
00:43:52,690 --> 00:43:55,980
I've given you meat and wine and music,

526
00:43:55,980 --> 00:43:58,820
but I haven't shown you

527
00:43:58,820 --> 00:44:01,490
the hospitality you deserve.

528
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:04,370
My king has married

529
00:44:04,370 --> 00:44:07,300
and I owe my new queen a wedding gift.

530
00:44:12,920 --> 00:44:13,760
Robb!

531
00:45:01,780 --> 00:45:04,120
You ready to head home to Winterfell, right?

532
00:45:07,630 --> 00:45:09,040
Feast over yet, is it?

533
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:10,760
Aye, it's over.

534
00:45:41,960 --> 00:45:43,050
Follow him.

535
00:45:46,290 --> 00:45:46,850
Aim!

536
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:18,150
It's too late.

537
00:47:00,250 --> 00:47:03,380
The King in the North arises.

538
00:47:25,130 --> 00:47:26,590
Lord Walder!

539
00:47:27,010 --> 00:47:28,580
Lord Walder, enough!

540
00:47:29,290 --> 00:47:30,820
Let it end!

541
00:47:33,130 --> 00:47:34,230
Please.

542
00:47:34,900 --> 00:47:36,740
He is my son.

543
00:47:37,540 --> 00:47:39,650
My first son.

544
00:47:39,650 --> 00:47:42,340
Let him go and I swear that we will forget this.

545
00:47:42,340 --> 00:47:44,590
I swear it by the old gods and new.

546
00:47:44,810 --> 00:47:46,420
We will take no vengeance.

547
00:47:46,420 --> 00:47:49,970
You already swore me one oath right here in my castle.

548
00:47:49,970 --> 00:47:53,820
You swore by all the gods your son would marry my daughter!

549
00:47:53,820 --> 00:47:57,160
Take me for a hostage, but let Robb go.

550
00:47:57,160 --> 00:47:59,020
Robb, get up.

551
00:47:59,540 --> 00:48:01,180
Get up and walk out.

552
00:48:02,020 --> 00:48:03,240
Please!

553
00:48:05,090 --> 00:48:06,530
Please!

554
00:48:07,990 --> 00:48:11,790
And why would I let him do that?

555
00:48:14,730 --> 00:48:17,030
On my honor as a Tully,

556
00:48:17,620 --> 00:48:19,960
on my honor as a Stark,

557
00:48:20,850 --> 00:48:22,590
let him go

558
00:48:23,120 --> 00:48:26,090
or I will cut your wife's throat.

559
00:48:34,550 --> 00:48:36,190
I'll find another.

560
00:48:40,120 --> 00:48:41,260
Mother.

561
00:48:43,510 --> 00:48:45,650
The Lannisters send their regards.

